  "name": "Wide Chord Stab",
  "author": "Riddim Rack",
  "description": "A short, bright chord hit with a quick filter close, a touch of warm saturation and a wide unison spread, built to answer a bass note on the drop. Play stacked triads on the beat; it is polyphonic, and harder hits play louder and open the filter wider. Macros: Snap pushes the filter snap harder and longer; Decay stretches each hit; Width spreads the stereo image; Space brings in reverb (the stab is dry until you turn it up).",
